    description: "**Defect (identity:F7 callable-kind sibling of WI-rihob).** Callable-kind *declarations* emit `stable_id=None` in several analyzers because their producer never computes a typed stable_id for them. Distinct from WI-rihob (done, PR #699), which backstopped the container/declaration kinds (class/struct/enum/trait/protocol/contract) with a name-scoped `make_declaration_stable_id`. Callable kinds must NOT use that name-scoped backstop — a name-only key collides across overloads — so they need a **typed** stable_id (`make_typed_stable_id`, keyed on the normalized signature) at the producer, exactly as concrete methods/functions already get.\n\n**Measure-live (2026-07-17, dev 5b8a44805f, post-WI-rihob):** on a 3-file fixture (go/solidity/rust surveyed via `hypergumbo survey`):\n- solidity `function` (`Token.mint`) → **stable_id=None**\n- solidity `constructor` (`Token.constructor`) → **stable_id=None**\n- go interface-method declaration (`Drawer.Draw`) → **stable_id=None**\n- (control) go concrete struct-method `Shape.Area` → HAS a typed id; rust struct/enum/trait, solidity contract, go struct/interface → all populated (WI-rihob).\n\nSo the residual is narrower than the original WI-rihob discussion's \"26 nodes\" list implied: the container kinds are now fixed; what remains is **callable declarations without a body-derived signature** — solidity `function`/`constructor` (likely `event`/`modifier` too — not yet measured), and go **interface-method** declarations (concrete methods already resolve).\n\n**Contract.** `stable_id` is the spec's signature-based rename/move survival key for typed languages. A solidity function or a go interface method is exactly the kind of typed callable that should carry one; null is reserved for true unavailability, not a producer omission.\n\n**Fix shape.** At each producer site, compute `make_typed_stable_id(kind, normalize_<lang>_signature(sig), name=…, qualified_name=…, file_stable_id=…)` — the same call the concrete-method/function sites already use. solidity.py: function/constructor (+ verify event/modifier). js_ts/go: the interface-method declaration path (grep the site that builds the interface-method Symbol with `shape_id=` but no `stable_id=`). Add per-analyzer producer tests (non-None + overload-distinct) — a name-only key would collide on overloaded solidity functions, which is why the typed tier is required.\n\n**Not this item.** The container/declaration kinds (WI-rihob, done). The non-canonical-format `stable_id=Symbol.id` reuse family across ~17 doc/config analyzers (WI-banod — a FORMAT gap, not a NULL gap).\n\n**Measure the full callable-null set before scoping the PR** — the fixture here proves the three cited cases; a fleet-wide survey (dogfood on a polyglot corpus) may surface more callable kinds (e.g. solidity event/modifier, other-language interface/abstract-method decls). Grep seed: `grep -n 'kind=\"function\"\\|kind=\"constructor\"\\|kind=\"method\"' packages/*/src/**/*.py` then check which sites omit `stable_id=`."  # 64bf
